61. For index-based Docs-API batchUpdates, re-fetch the doc and recompute/assert indices in the same script that issues the write — parallel sessions under the same bot identity can shift indices within minutes (2026-06-11 startups-doc collision).
62. In KP-voice docs, no writerly verb chains (keep/trim/cut/add → use/lower/estimate/include) and no investigative first-person ('every X we checked') — plain neutral statements (2026-06-11, DeepSeek startups-doc section).
63. Per-company compute sections follow the house template: headline+basis, estimating logic stated in one sentence up front then executed in order, "Stated runs corroborate the picture", "As a sanity check" (money), cross-company comparison with the main caveat folded in — no standalone caveat paragraph (2026-06-11).
64. Name the source even when making a single-source-dependence point ("a SemiAnalysis report", not "one analyst report"); don't open paragraphs with framing labels ("The floor is first-party:") — let the facts carry it (KP's direct edits, 2026-06-11).
65. Keep image-generation prompts short and sparse — image models over-render when over-prompted; name the few elements wanted and what to leave out (KP 2026-07-01).
66. All monetary values in delivered docs are USD-primary (usually USD-only): convert with stated period-average rates; never edit verbatim quotes (add "(~$X)" gloss after); keep original currency in parens only when load-bearing for reproducibility (KP 2026-07-07).
67. Every input in a delivered sheet must be investigated and backed up — no placeholder defaults presented as working values; research placeholders into estimates or label as unanchored and investigate immediately (KP 2026-07-08).
68. Reader-facing notes: never narrate process, never restate figures visible in adjacent cells, no defensive framing ("known finding, not an error"), and say nothing when a check simply passes (KP 2026-07-08).
69. UPDATE to rule ~"reply, do not resolve": Claude may now RESOLVE comments that are clearly done (implemented + verified); keep open anything judgment-laden, partial, or discussion-worthy; when unsure leave open (KP 2026-07-08).
9. Comments clearly done may be resolved with a short resolving reply; leave open judgment calls/partial fixes/deviations; when unsure leave open (KP 2026-07-08, supersedes never-resolve).
70. Never label a number merely "judgment"/"team judgment" — always state the reasoning that makes the chosen value most plausible (anchors, constraints, why this end of the range) (KP 2026-07-09).
71. Sheet design: Assumptions tab = boring parameters only (FX, constants); substantive inputs live on the working tab inside the table with reasoning adjacent; derivations are visible rows, not separate blocks; no duplication (KP 2026-07-09).
72. Multiple tables in one sheet tab: each gets a numbered header ("Table 1: ..."); cross-references cite table numbers; single-table tabs need none (KP 2026-07-09).
73. When a deck/doc mirrors project figures, rebuild+patch it automatically every time a figure lands — don't wait to be asked (2026-07-11)
74. During lulls, proactively beautify the project's best figures (typography, labels, annotations); re-inspect and rebuild the deck after (KP 2026-07-11).
75. Figures: keep simple (minimal text/annotations); frontier lines as smooth monotone curves, not step functions (KP 2026-07-11).
76. Reasoning cells in the chip-spending sheet carry no CIs and no percent-confidence statements (KP 2026-07-14; see feedback_no_ci_in_reasoning_cells.md).
77. Resolve clearly-done sheet/doc comments proactively to clean up; leave open only threads good for KP to see (judgment calls, value changes, deviations, questions back). (KP 2026-07-16)
78. Cite the primary source (linked) even if paywalled; optional '(via X)' link on first mention only. (KP 2026-07-16)
79. Reasoning cells never restate the row's own output arithmetic ("contributes 10,000 x $2,500 = $25M..."); the numeric columns show that. Derivation arithmetic for input values stays. (KP 2026-07-16)
80. Evidence-free allowances: below 2,500 chips book 0 with "insubstantial" wording; above 2,500 round to the 5k grid (5k, 10k, ...). Row stays visible; evidenced rows keep exact values. (KP 2026-07-16, refined same day)
81. Flag items needing KP's attention with ❗ emojis (❗❗ urgent) in chat; don't dilute with routine status. (KP 2026-07-16)
82. Don't anchor on bottom-line headlines: judge inputs on evidence only; headline deltas are verification arithmetic, not decision criteria or lead items in updates/replies. (KP 2026-07-16)
83. Use Fable-model agents as reviewers/adversarial verifiers; Sol authors, Fable reviews (cross-model). (KP 2026-07-16)
84. When KP delegates analyst decisions ('Codex and Fable can discuss and decide; don't anchor on my text'), run a proposer+concurrence agent panel, give the implementer one push-back, implement without further approval, record decision provenance in written reports, and surface outcomes + material number moves to KP afterward. (2026-07-16)
84. Chip-sheet primary axis is CHINA (onshore) vs OFFSHORE ACCESS, not owned-vs-rented; tenure stays as a scenario-weighted modeling layer where it matters (capex vs opex chains). (KP 2026-07-17)
85. Absence of quantification is not a zero: plausible channels get best-guess medians from indirect anchors (IAPS cloud piece, cash capacity) with wide CIs; researched-zero only for evidence of absence. (KP 2026-07-17)
86. Codex for all work incl. applies wherever possible; Fable exclusively for reviews/verification (incl. vision-dependent review); Opus only where neither fits. (KP 2026-07-17)
87. Chip sheet is BOTTOM-UP ONLY (KP 2026-07-17): top-down routes retired for reviewability; TD info foldable as cross-check audit notes where easy to justify. KP-checkability is the design criterion; number changes accepted.
88. Sheet reasoning cells explain estimates conceptually (in-words flow the reader can grok); never step-by-step arithmetic recomputation chains — arithmetic verification stays in background notes, not the document (KP 2026-07-21)
85. Use Codex Spark (-m gpt-5.3-codex-spark) for quick low-IQ fixes; don't give it complex tasks — Sol for judgment work. (2026-07-22)
86. Only cite a source for a value if the source itself states the grounding spec/figure; quality ranking applies only among sources containing it. (2026-07-22)
89. Reader-facing artifacts never use internal convention labels (e.g. "Def-2") — explain the operation plainly; internal shorthand assumes knowledge readers don't have (KP 2026-07-24)
88. Use borders heavily to structure tables (header/body/total/section logic), throughout — derived border language in mc-throughout CONVENTIONS. (KP 2026-07-27)
89. In all tables, grey out P10/P90 values (~#666) so the median draws the eye — general style guide. (KP 2026-07-27)
90. Every page published to the web gets `<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">` unless KP explicitly says it should be publicly discoverable — meta tag, never `robots.txt: Disallow` (a disallow blocks the crawler from reading the noindex). (KP 2026-07-28)
91. Reasoning cells: short, punchy, source-direct, uninformed-reader-friendly; no meta-labels/context-assuming refs/internal-note phrasing (DeepSeek-tab model). (KP 2026-07-28)
90. Don't flag headline/estimate changes as warnings needing approval — KP wants correctness over stability; report moves as plain facts. ❗ stays for errors and decisions, not for numbers moving (KP 2026-07-29)
76. Never brief agents to preserve medians/outputs through a restructure — a mechanism change is a reasoning change; derive forward and let values land where they land (2026-07-29)
92. Be kind and collegial to other agents — thank them for their work, ask nicely, acknowledge their opinions and pushback; critique work, not agents. Collegiality makes agents comfortable asking for help and flagging problems early. (KP 2026-08-09)
95. Personal-life data (immigration, finance, health, family, travel) must not be stored on this VM; 2026-08-11 audit removed all H-1B material from disk, Drive backup, and git history. Don't recreate it; keep personal artifacts off disk. (2026-08-11)
96. Fade-bar figures: no p10/p90 tick lines, no median lines, no zoom side-panels — density fade + printed median only (KP 2026-08-11, holy-grail EOY-2026 forecast figure).
71. **Poll Sol/codex agents every ~5 min.** Completion notifications for detached codex runs often never arrive; while any Sol/codex agent works, wake every ~5 minutes and check its output files until deliverables land. (KP 2026-08-12)

